    "result_text": "All tests pass (`BUILD SUCCESS`). Here's a summary of the change.\n\n## What I did\n\nReplaced the string `membershipTier` with a numeric `membershipLevel` (1\u20133), computed on creation as *start at 1, +1 for an email, +1 when `namesakeCount` is 0, capped at 3*. The old tier's `GOLD`-for-large-household behavior is gone, so I also removed the now-dead household-size machinery that only fed it.\n\n**Files changed:**\n\n- **`model/Owner.java`** \u2014 Replaced `getMembershipTier()` (String) with `getMembershipLevel()` (int): `1 + email? + uniqueName?`, `Math.min(\u2026, 3)`. Removed the `householdSize` field and its getter/setter, which existed solely to drive the old `GOLD` tier.\n- **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 Replaced the `membershipTier` (string) response property with `membershipLevel` (integer, `minimum: 1`, read-only). This regenerates `OwnerDto`, and MapStruct maps it by name.\n- **`function/owner/AuditOwnerCreated.java`** \u2014 The create audit line now records `membershipLevel=` in place of the tier (the spec's \"record the level instead\").\n- **`function/owner/FlagHouseholdSize.java`** \u2014 Deleted; its only consumer (the GOLD tier) is gone.\n- **`officefloor/rest/api/owners.POST.yml`** and **`owners/{ownerId}.GET.yml`** \u2014 Removed the `householdSize` pipeline step, rewiring `bulkWarning \u2192 respond`.\n\nThe new test `AcceptanceTest.coreNumericLevel` (email + unique name \u2192 level 3, capped) passes, as does the full suite. The audit output confirms it live: `AUDIT - Owner created id=11 customerCode=TOW-LEV-0001 registrationDate=2026-10-05 membershipLevel=3`.\n\n## One judgment call worth flagging\n\nThe spec says *\"anything that recorded the tier (such as the create audit line) must record the level instead.\"* In this codebase the audit line did **not** previously record the tier (it only logged id/customerCode/registrationDate), and no test asserts on it. I read the spec as authoritative that the audit is a tier-recorder and added `membershipLevel` to it. If you'd rather leave the audit line untouched, that's a one-line revert.\n\n`membershipLevel` is a derived transient (like the old tier) rather than a persisted column, since it's fully determined by the already-persisted `email` and `namesakeCount` \u2014 so no schema change was needed. The spec's \"level 4 is reserved for tenure\" isn't implemented here (tenure is out of scope); the cap is 3.",
