    "final_verdict": "VERDICT: LGTM\n\nThe change is structurally clean and idiomatic for this codebase:\n\n- **Logic lives in the right unit.** The level derivation replaces the old tier derivation in the exact same place (`Owner.getMembershipLevel()`, a `@Transient` derived getter), mirroring the prior `getMembershipTier()` convention. A maintainer would find it in the natural spot.\n- **Dead code removed cleanly, not left orphaned.** Because `membershipLevel` no longer depends on household size, the author correctly deleted the now-unused `householdSize` field/accessors on `Owner`, the entire `FlagHouseholdSize` function class, and the `householdSize` pipeline steps in both `owners.POST.yml` and `owners/{ownerId}.GET.yml` (including their explanatory comments). Nothing is left dangling or half-wired.\n- **No duplication / no catch-all.** The derivation is a single small method; the audit side effect stays in `AuditOwnerCreated` (just extended to carry the new field), keeping it out of the responder \u2014 consistent with the existing step responsibilities.\n- **Docs and OpenAPI kept in step** with the code (javadoc, schema type/field rename, example), so the contract surface stays coherent.\n\nNo structural improvements needed.",
